course: dictionary
lesson: 7401
title: Podium: a raised stand for speakers and winners
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A podium is a small raised platform that a person stands on, so everyone can see and hear them. Speakers, music conductors and prize winners all use one. «Leaders do not have to take part in debates; when one declines, a channel may show an empty podium, an "empty chair".» The word empty tells you nobody is standing there, and the sentence says the empty podium stands for a leader who said no.
explain: Context gives you clues. Look at the words around podium: debates, declines, channel, empty. A podium is a place where people stand to be seen, so a platform with nobody on it sends a message. Try your meaning in the sentence: "an empty platform" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: In sport, the podium is a stand with three steps. The first-place winner stands in the middle, the highest step. Second place stands on one side and third place on the other. "To get on the podium" means to finish in the top three.
fact: A podium is a small raised platform that a person stands on.
fact: A podium can hold a speaker, a music conductor or a prize winner.
fact: In the Olympics, first place stands in the middle, second on one side and third on the other.
fact: «To get on the podium» means to finish in the top three.
fact: In the US, a podium can also mean a lectern, the stand that holds a speaker's notes.
exercise: What does podium mean? | *A small raised platform | A kind of musical instrument | A large room for dancing | A type of boat
exercise: In the Olympics, which place stands in the middle of the podium? | Fourth | Second | *First | Third
exercise: Ben says «to get on the podium» means to be on stage in a play. What does it really mean? | To win a game of chess | To stand very still | To be late for lessons | *To finish in the top three
test: The Olympic podium has three steps. Which winner stands on the highest step? | Last | *First | Third | Second
test: «Leaders do not have to take part in debates; when one declines, a channel may show an empty podium, an "empty chair".» What does declines mean here? | Makes a loud noise | *Says no and does not take part | Falls over | Says yes and joins in
exam: «Leaders do not have to take part in debates; when one declines, a channel may show an empty podium, an "empty chair".» What is the empty podium showing? | *That a leader chose not to take part | That the leader is late | That the podium is broken | That a new chair has arrived
